hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16518","Waki narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham al-Attar narrated to us, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, and he once said: He heard him from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named me Yusuf and wiped over my head."
"16519","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Nadr ibn Qays, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named me Yusuf."
"16520","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to a man of the Ansar and his wife: Perform Umrah in Ramadan, for indeed an Umrah in Ramadan for you two is like a Hajj; and Sufyan once said, and he did not say: He narrated to me, meaning Ibn al-Munkadir: For indeed an Umrah therein is like a Hajj."
"16521","He said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: I heard Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seated me in his lap and wiped over my head and named me Yusuf, he said:"
"16522","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abdullah ibn Miskin informed us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, and he mentioned the preceding hadith."
